# CLAUDE.local.md — private overlay

**Gitignored.** Project-private supplement to `CLAUDE.md`. Claude
Code auto-loads this; the public repo never sees it. Workspace backup:
`tick-trader-percore-workspace/CLAUDE.local.md.backup` via
`/sync-workspace`.

**This file is an INDEX.** Each rule = one-line statement + one-line
trigger + canonical-doc pointer. Deep-dive bodies (Why + How to
apply + worked examples + anti-patterns) live in:

- `tick-trader-percore-workspace/DESIGN_SPECS/<pattern>.md` — pattern bodies
- `DOCS/RECURRING_BUG_PATTERNS.md` — bug class registry
- `DOCS/TECH_DEBT.md`, `DOCS/PARITY_ISSUES.md`, `FEATURE_LOOKUP.md` — auto-write ledgers
- `~/.claude/projects/-home-caramel-code-FoxML-Trader-v2/memory/` — feedback / user / project memories
- `tick-trader-percore-workspace/claude-skills/<skill>/SKILL.md` — operational contracts
- `tick-trader-percore-workspace/DOCS/LANDMINES.md` — operational pitfalls
- `CLAUDE.md` items 1-30 — codified design philosophy (always loaded)

Skills that fire on relevant work load matching DESIGN_SPECS bodies
dynamically — see "Skill load contracts" below.

---

## Required reading before performance-sensitive code

| Doc | Trigger — read it BEFORE writing or editing... |
|---|---|
| `DOCS/STRATEGY_AND_CODING_RULES.md` | any code in hot path, slow path, OMS drainer, parsing, ML inference, strategies, RollingStats / RegimeSignals / ExecutionCore — i.e., anything in `CoreFrameworks/`, `Strategies/`, `ML_Headers/`, `DataStream/`, or `FixedPoint/`. 11 strict invariants (no malloc, no virtual, no mutex, no sleep_for, no atof/strstr in parsers, cache alignment, branchless, AVX-512-friendly layouts, SCHED_FIFO/isolcpus deployment). |
| `DOCS/LATENCY_OPTIMIZATION_AUDIT.md` | any optimization investigation, performance-regression triage. 13 parts, ~40 specific items: hot path, slow path SIMD, arch invariants, ingestion+ML+memory, system tail variance, allocator eradication, parsing, OMS variance, concurrency, FPN libs, HFT system ops, hardware/OS tuning. |
| `plans/_cross-cutting/2026-05-06-latency-path-discipline.md` | any modification to **any code on a latency-impacting path**: hot path (`ExecutionCore_Tick`, `BG_Evaluate`, `SG_Evaluate`, `GateParameters`, `ParameterSlot`), slow path (`EventLoop_RebuildOneCore`, `RollingStats_Push`, `Regime_ComputeSignals`), OMS drainer (`OMS_DrainSubmit`, `OrderManager_Tick`), producer fan-out, snapshot publish, parsing. 7 architectural rules scaled by cadence + anti-pattern history + pre-merge verification checklist. |

**Workflow:** open the rules doc first, scan relevant sections, then
write code. The audit doc is consulted when the rule is "yes but how"
— it has concrete per-site suggestions with file:line refs. The
hot-path discipline doc is the third leg — read when touching hot-path
layout / per-tick code.

---

## Auto-write contracts

When an audit / skill / sub-ship surfaces an item below, the agent
MUST write the entry to the named ledger. Operator reviews at boundary;
agent does mechanical bookkeeping. Don't bury in chat / code comments
/ postmortems — those rotate or get compacted.

| Surface | Ledger | Trigger |
|---|---|---|
| Parity findings | `DOCS/PARITY_ISSUES.md` | `/parity-check` or any audit naming a parity surface |
| Deferred items | `DOCS/TECH_DEBT.md` | `/readiness` Check 25, `/merge-scan`, scope-discussion deferrals |
| Operator-visible features | `tick-trader-percore-workspace/FEATURE_LOOKUP.md` | New cfg flag / observability surface / persistence file / boot gate / training knob / fallback path at sub-ship close |
| Decoupling positioning | `plans/_future/2026-05-12-decoupling-endgoal-roadmap.md` | Any ship touching GUI ↔ runtime, TUISnapshot, CLI mode dispatch, cfg ownership, logging path |
| Cohort-audit findings | `DOCS/TECH_DEBT.md` | New boolean cfg field with 2+ siblings → cohort eligibility per `DESIGN_SPECS/cfg-flag-eligibility-criteria.md` |
| Operational landmines | `tick-trader-percore-workspace/DOCS/LANDMINES.md` | Non-obvious pitfall (segfault / race / library quirk) that took >1h to debug |

**FEATURE_LOOKUP entry template:** `### <name> (vX.Y.Z+)` → **What** /
**Cfg flags** / **Fallback** / **Where to verify** (panel field /
log line / file with file:line refs) / **Paper-test sanity** / **Gotchas** /
**Related**. Skip auto-write for: pure refactors, internal helper
extraction, bug fixes restoring expected behavior, bytewise-identical
perf optimizations.

